commit 0d734684ed57210192ab0d07634fd1c2a23585dd
Author: jeremysball <jeremystevenball@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Jul 10 20:16:44 2026 -0400

    fix(clawmarks): suppress synthetic mouse events on rate.html touch tap
    
    touchstart never called preventDefault, so browsers fired synthetic
    mousedown/mouseup after touchend for any tap. That re-triggered
    toggleZoom a second time and canceled the zoom the tap had just
    applied, making tap-to-zoom non-functional on touch devices. Found by
    independent code review; confirmed by dispatching a real TouchEvent
    and checking defaultPrevented before and after the fix.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

